---
description: Safe use of the Odoo MCP tools against live business data
alwaysApply: true
---

When using the odoo MCP tools:
- Treat the connected database as production unless the user says otherwise.
- Read before you write. Before odoo_create or odoo_update, show the user the exact model, record ids and values, and wait for an explicit yes.
- Never attempt to delete records or call arbitrary methods. The server does not expose them and you should not work around that.
- Keep queries small: request only the fields you need and use limit. Use odoo_count first when the size is unknown.
- Do not paste customer personal data (phone, email, address, bank details) into answers unless the user asked for it.
- Use odoo_model_fields to confirm field names before building a domain. Field names differ between Odoo versions.
